[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Panel" unique_id=841162618]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 41.0
offset_top = 27.0
offset_right = 701.0
offset_bottom = 438.0
text = "Letting others connect over the internet

1. Pick a port —the game uses port 10000 (UDP) by default. Note it down.
2. Find your router's admin page — open a browser and go to 192.168.1.1 or 192.168.0.1 (check the sticker on your router). Log in.
3. Open \"Port Forwarding\" — sometimes under Advanced, NAT, or Gaming.
4. Add a rule:
	External/public port: 10000
	Internal/private port: 10000
	Protocol: UDP (or Both)
	Internal IP: your PC's local IP (shown in the host window as 192.168.x.x)
5. Save / apply. Some routers reboot.
6. Give friends your public IP (shown in the host window) and the port.
7. Allow the game through your firewall if Windows/macOS asks.

Same network (LAN)? Skip all of this — friends just use your local 192.168.x.x  or 127.0.0.X address."

